<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: assad_hamid_toilet_meme; hasOverallIntent: toxicity_harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a child standing in a bathroom with toilet paper strewn across the floor and sink, implying a messy or 'exploded' state. The text overlay reads 'assad: my son exploded better than yours, lol' and 'hamid:'. This is a meme that uses a visual of a child's chaotic bathroom scene to imply a competitive, boastful, or mocking comparison between two individuals (likely named Assad and Hamid). The intent is to create humor through absurdity and exaggeration, but the phrase 'exploded' in the context of a child's bathroom is potentially harmful as it could be interpreted as a crude or vulgar reference to bodily functions or messiness. The meme may be intended to be funny or sarcastic, but the use of 'exploded' in a context involving children and bodily mess can be seen as insensitive or potentially offensive, especially if it implies a crude or vulgar comparison. The overall intent is to provoke laughter through shock value and absurd comparison, but the content may be perceived as harmful due to its crude or vulgar undertones."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#toxicity_1> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionMethod> "llm_extraction_huggingface" .
