<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'assad: my son exploded better than yours, lol' explicitly refers to the child in the image as 'my son'. The visual material of the child standing in the messy bathroom is thus mapped onto the textual entity 'my son', creating an analogical mapping where the child represents Assad's son in the competitive boast."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#EnvironmentalText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DiegeticallyIntegrated> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DiegeticallyIntegrated> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text that exists as part of the fictional or depicted world within memes"@en .
_:nca66f29bc1864c069056b7d4ba722d66b39 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Value> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One dimension embodying certain values versus another dimension embodying opposing values in memes, e.g. text and visuals representing conflicting moral or aesthetic values"@en .
