_:nca66f29bc1864c069056b7d4ba722d66b64 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
_:nca66f29bc1864c069056b7d4ba722d66b27 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#bodily_function_stereotype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The use of the word 'exploded' in the context of a child's bathroom is a crude or vulgar reference to bodily functions or messiness. This requires background knowledge of cultural stereotypes and crude humor to understand the meme's potential toxicity and offensive nature."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TemplateStructure> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Template Structure elements from the image. Template Structure includes: template patterns, organizational frameworks, structural elements, layout templates, framework components, and structural patterns. For each structural element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'contrast_template', 'layout_framework'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the contrast template', 'the layout framework'), 3) A brief description of the structural pattern or framework. Focus on the underlying organizational structure of the meme. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"contrast_template\", \"label\": \"the contrast template\", \"description\": \"The meme follows a contrast template with calm foreground subject against chaotic background scene\"}"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#horizontallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:nca66f29bc1864c069056b7d4ba722d66b43 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#EnvironmentalText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text naturally occurring in the depicted meme scene environment"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#perspectivallyContradicting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "perspectivally contradicting"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#environmentallyTextualIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "environmentally textual in"@en .
