<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the child in the image, as the text 'assad: my son exploded better than yours, lol' explicitly refers to the child as 'my son'. The user, as the viewer of the meme, is implicitly positioned as the one who might be responding to Assad's boast, thus projecting themselves onto the child as the 'son' being compared. The child is visually mapped onto the textual entity 'my son', creating a semiotic projection where the user sees themselves as the owner or parent of the child in the image, thereby aligning with the competitive boast in the text."@en .
